Teaching, apprenticeship, and assessment (@teaching-apprenticeship-and-assessment: 0, is #chapter, #outline) { r_757VJ3M3MM162D3AEZ2TWFSSQM
Teaching reproduces a society's ability to understand and perform skilled work. This material covers prerequisites, explanations, practice, feedback, demonstrations, supervised experience, and assessment, including transferring tacit expertise and training the next teachers, researchers, technicians, and operators.

**Common foundation developed:** [Learning capabilities and evidence](../../core/Define-what-someone-should-be-able-to-understand-and-do.lingua) begins nine connected lessons through assessment, transfer and practical handover. This is a shared foundation; full teaching, apprenticeship, tacit expertise and observed supervised practice remain pending.

**Parent:** [Learning and teaching](../Learning-and-teaching.lingua#r_1JERVDF9ND9GX4T1AGV0PE1HT3).
